{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Bell number B_n for a given non-negative integer 'n'.\n    B_n represents the number of ways to partition a set of 'n' elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _calculate_bell_number_dp(n)\n\n\ndef _calculate_bell_number_dp(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Helper function to compute the Bell number B_n using dynamic programming\n    based on Stirling numbers of the second kind.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # stirling_dp[i][j] stores Stirling numbers of the second kind S(i, j).\n    # S(i, j) is the number of ways to partition a set of i elements into j non-empty subsets.\n    stirling_dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case for Stirling numbers: S(0, 0) = 1\n    stirling_dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for Stirling numbers S(i, j) using the recurrence:\n    # S(i, j) = S(i-1, j-1) + j * S(i-1, j)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            stirling_dp[i][j] = stirling_dp[i-1][j-1] + j * stirling_dp[i-1][j]\n            \n    # The Bell number B_n is the sum of Stirling numbers of the second kind S(n, k) for k from 0 to n.\n    bell_n = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        bell_n += stirling_dp[n][k]\n\n    return bell_n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "def is_samepatterns(words, patterns):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a sequence of words follows a given pattern sequence, establishing a consistent one-to-one mapping.\n    Ensures bidirectional mapping consistency for all occurrences of elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(words) != len(patterns):\n        return False\n\n    word_to_pattern_map = {}\n    pattern_to_word_map = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(words)):\n        word = words[i]\n        pattern = patterns[i]\n\n        # Check word to pattern consistency\n        if word in word_to_pattern_map:\n            if word_to_pattern_map[word] != pattern:\n                return False\n        else:\n            word_to_pattern_map[word] = pattern\n\n        # Check pattern to word consistency\n        if pattern in pattern_to_word_map:\n            if pattern_to_word_map[pattern] != word:\n                return False\n        else:\n            pattern_to_word_map[pattern] = word\n\n    return True"}
