{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is undulating, meaning its digits strictly alternate between two distinct digits.\n    Returns True if undulating, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = str(number)\n    n = len(s)\n\n    if n < 2:  # Single-digit numbers are not undulating\n        return False\n\n    # Find the first two distinct digits\n    digit1 = s[0]\n    digit2 = None\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if s[i] != digit1:\n            digit2 = s[i]\n            break\n    \n    if digit2 is None: # All digits are the same (e.g., 333)\n        return False\n\n    # Check for strict alternation\n    for i in range(n):\n        if i % 2 == 0:  # Even position should be digit1\n            if s[i] != digit1:\n                return False\n        else:  # Odd position should be digit2\n            if s[i] != digit2:\n                return False\n                \n    return True"}
