{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-positioned bits (0-indexed) of the input integer to 1.\n    This is achieved by iterating through common bit positions and applying a bitwise OR operation.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = number\n    # Iterate through bit positions. A 64-bit integer covers a wide range.\n    for p in range(64):\n        if p % 2 == 0:  # Check if the position is even\n            # Create a bitmask for the current even position and set the bit\n            result = result | (1 << p)\n    return result"}
