{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def _calculate_increasing_sums(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Helper function to calculate the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at each index.\n    result[i] is the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at arr[i].\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n    lis_sums = [float(x) for x in arr]\n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lis_sums[i] = max(lis_sums[i], lis_sums[j] + arr[i])\n    return lis_sums\n\ndef _calculate_decreasing_sums(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Helper function to calculate the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at each index.\n    result[i] is the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at arr[i].\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n    lds_sums = [float(x) for x in arr]\n\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lds_sums[i] = max(lds_sums[i], lds_sums[j] + arr[i])\n    return lds_sums\n\ndef max_sum(arr: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array.\n    A sequence is bitonic if it is first strictly increasing and then strictly decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0.0\n\n    lis_sums = _calculate_increasing_sums(arr)\n    lds_sums = _calculate_decreasing_sums(arr)\n\n    max_overall_sum = 0.0\n    for i in range(n):\n        # The peak element arr[i] is included in both LIS and LDS sum calculations.\n        # It must be subtracted once to get the correct total bitonic subsequence sum.\n        current_bitonic_sum = lis_sums[i] + lds_sums[i] - arr[i]\n        max_overall_sum = max(max_overall_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_overall_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    This implementation uses dynamic programming.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n\n    # An empty string has an LPS length of 0.\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the LPS for the substring s[i...j].\n    dp = [[0 for _ in range(n)] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromes of length 1.\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for substrings of length 2 to n.\n    # 'gap' represents the length of the substring minus 1.\n    for gap in range(1, n):\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            j = i + gap\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If outer characters match, they contribute 2 to the LPS.\n                # If gap is 1 (substring of length 2 like \"aa\"), dp[i+1][j-1] refers to an empty string (length 0).\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + (dp[i+1][j-1] if gap > 1 else 0)\n            else:\n                # If outer characters don't match, take the maximum LPS by excluding\n                # either the left character or the right character.\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i+1][j], dp[i][j-1])\n\n    # The result is the LPS length for the entire string s[0...n-1].\n    return dp[0][n-1]"}
