{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "from typing import Sequence, Tuple, Union, List\n\nNumber = Union[int, float]\n\ndef maximize_elements(\n    collection_a: Sequence[Tuple[Number, Number]],\n    collection_b: Sequence[Tuple[Number, Number]]\n) -> List[Tuple[Number, Number]]:\n    \"\"\"Maximizes elements between two collections of two-element tuples.\n    It returns a new list of tuples where each element is the maximum of the\n    corresponding elements from collection_a and collection_b.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # The design context provides a _validate_input_collections helper,\n    # but the instructions state \"Do NOT call any helper that is not defined inline in your response\".\n    # Given the constraint, validation logic must be integrated directly, but the prompt\n    # also states \"Do NOT add isinstance() checks or raise exceptions for edge cases\"\n    # for the generated code. Therefore, assuming valid input as per the problem's\n    # initial assertion and removing explicit checks that would be\n    # in _validate_input_collections if it were allowed.\n\n    result_collection: List[Tuple[Number, Number]] = []\n    for i in range(len(collection_a)):\n        tuple_a = collection_a[i]\n        tuple_b = collection_b[i]\n\n        max_first = max(tuple_a[0], tuple_b[0])\n        max_second = max(tuple_a[1], tuple_b[1])\n        result_tuple = (max_first, max_second)\n        result_collection.append(result_tuple)\n\n    return result_collection"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/260", "solution": "def newman_prime(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Newman-Shanks-Williams number S_n.\n    The problem implies S_n will be prime for valid inputs 'n'.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1  # S_0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1  # S_1\n\n    s_prev = 1  # Corresponds to S_{k-2}\n    s_curr = 1  # Corresponds to S_{k-1}\n\n    # Iterate from k=2 up to n to calculate S_n\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        s_next = 2 * s_curr + s_prev\n        s_prev = s_curr\n        s_curr = s_next\n\n    return s_curr"}
