{"task_id": "Mbpp/406", "solution": "def find_Parity(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if the parity (count of set bits) of a given number is odd.\n    Returns True if the count of set bits is odd, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert the number to its binary string representation and count the '1's.\n    # This approach correctly handles both positive and negative integers in Python\n    # by counting set bits in their standard string representation (e.g., '0b1100' or '-0b101').\n    set_bit_count = bin(number).count('1')\n    \n    # Return True if the count of set bits is odd, False otherwise.\n    return set_bit_count % 2 == 1"}
