{"task_id": "Mbpp/418", "solution": "def Find_Max(input_list: list) -> any:\n    \"\"\"Finds the element of a list having the maximum length. Returns None if the input list is empty.\"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return None\n\n    max_element = input_list[0]\n    max_len = len(input_list[0])\n\n    for element in input_list[1:]:\n        current_len = len(element)\n        if current_len > max_len:\n            max_len = current_len\n            max_element = element\n            \n    return max_element"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(numbers: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the pair of integers with the highest product from a given array.\n\n    The function sorts the array to identify the two largest numbers and the two smallest numbers,\n    then compares the product of these pairs to determine the highest product.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Assuming the input list has at least two elements as per design context and problem constraints.\n    # Sort the array in ascending order.\n    numbers.sort()\n\n    # Product of the two largest numbers (positive product potential)\n    product_of_largest_two = numbers[-1] * numbers[-2]\n    pair_of_largest_two = (numbers[-2], numbers[-1])\n\n    # Product of the two smallest numbers (positive product potential if both are negative)\n    product_of_smallest_two = numbers[0] * numbers[1]\n    pair_of_smallest_two = (numbers[0], numbers[1])\n\n    if product_of_largest_two >= product_of_smallest_two:\n        return pair_of_largest_two\n    else:\n        return pair_of_smallest_two"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/419", "solution": "def round_and_sum(numbers: list[float]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Rounds each number in the list, sums them, and multiplies by list length.\n    Returns the final integer result.\"\"\"\n    list_length = len(numbers)\n    sum_of_rounded_numbers = 0\n\n    for number in numbers:\n        rounded_number = round(number)\n        sum_of_rounded_numbers += rounded_number\n\n    final_result = sum_of_rounded_numbers * list_length\n    return final_result"}
