{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    Operates on a copy of the input list to maintain immutability.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    # Create a copy to ensure the original array is not modified\n    sorted_arr = arr[:]\n\n    # Start with a large gap, then reduce the gap\n    gap = n // 2\n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = sorted_arr[i]\n            j = i\n            # Inner insertion sort for current gap\n            while j >= gap and sorted_arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                sorted_arr[j] = sorted_arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            sorted_arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n    return sorted_arr"}
