{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "import collections.abc\nfrom typing import Union\n\ndef index_multiplication(\n    tuple1: tuple[tuple[Union[int, float], Union[int, float]], ...],\\\n    tuple2: tuple[tuple[Union[int, float], Union[int, float]], ...]\\\n) -> tuple[tuple[Union[int, float], Union[int, float]], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs index-wise multiplication of tuple elements from two input tuples.\n    This function validates inputs and then computes the element-wise product.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _validate_input_tuple(input_tuple: tuple) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates if the input_tuple adheres to the expected structure.\n        Raises ValueError if validation fails.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(input_tuple, collections.abc.Sequence) or isinstance(input_tuple, (str, bytes)):\n            raise ValueError(\"Input must be a tuple.\")\n        for nested_tuple in input_tuple:\n            if not isinstance(nested_tuple, collections.abc.Sequence) or isinstance(nested_tuple, (str, bytes)):\n                raise ValueError(\"Nested elements must be tuples.\")\n            if len(nested_tuple) != 2:\n                raise ValueError(\"Nested tuples must contain exactly two elements.\")\n            for element in nested_tuple:\n                if not isinstance(element, (int, float)):\n                    raise ValueError(\"Elements within nested tuples must be numeric.\")\n\n    _validate_input_tuple(tuple1)\n    _validate_input_tuple(tuple2)\n\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same number of nested tuples.\")\n\n    result_list = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        nested_t1 = tuple1[i]\n        nested_t2 = tuple2[i]\n        \n        element1_result = nested_t1[0] * nested_t2[0]\n        element2_result = nested_t1[1] * nested_t2[1]\n        result_list.append((element1_result, element2_result))\n\n    return tuple(result_list)"}
