{"task_id": "Mbpp/476", "solution": "def big_sum(input_array: list) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of the largest and smallest values in a given array.\n    Assumes the input_array contains numerical values.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_array:\n        # Per design, no explicit error handling for empty array,\n        # but max/min on empty sequence raises ValueError.\n        # Returning 0 might be a reasonable default if empty array is an allowed input.\n        # For now, let Python's built-in functions handle it.\n        return 0 \n    \n    largest_value = max(input_array)\n    smallest_value = min(input_array)\n    return largest_value + smallest_value"}
