{"task_id": "Mbpp/557", "solution": "def toggle_string(input_string: str) -> str:\n    # Toggles the case of all alphabetic characters in the input string.\n    # Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged.\n    result_chars = []\n    for char in input_string:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            result_chars.append(chr(ord(char) - 32)) # Convert to uppercase\n        elif 'A' <= char <= 'Z':\n            result_chars.append(chr(ord(char) + 32)) # Convert to lowercase\n        else:\n            result_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "def find_Odd_Pair(input_list: list[int], length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of unique pairs in a list whose XOR sum is odd.\"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    for i in range(length - 1):\n        for j in range(i + 1, length):\n            xor_value = input_list[i] ^ input_list[j]\n            if xor_value % 2 != 0:\n                odd_count += 1\n    return odd_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum(input_list: list[int], length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of the largest contiguous sublist using Kadane's algorithm.\n    Handles lists with negative numbers correctly.\n    \"\"\"\n    if length == 0:\n        # Per design, handling empty lists is not a primary concern for initialization,\n        # but a robust solution would return 0 or raise an error for an empty list.\n        # For this context, assuming length > 0 or that a list of only negative numbers\n        # will be handled by returning the largest single negative number.\n        return 0 \n\n    current_max_sum = input_list[0]\n    global_max_sum = input_list[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, length):\n        current_max_sum = max(input_list[i], current_max_sum + input_list[i])\n        global_max_sum = max(global_max_sum, current_max_sum)\n\n    return global_max_sum"}
