{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "def digit_distance_nums(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the absolute per-digit differences between two integers.\n    The shorter number is padded with leading zeros for comparison.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_num1 = str(num1)\n    s_num2 = str(num2)\n\n    max_len = max(len(s_num1), len(s_num2))\n\n    s_num1 = s_num1.zfill(max_len)\n    s_num2 = s_num2.zfill(max_len)\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(max_len):\n        digit1 = int(s_num1[i])\n        digit2 = int(s_num2[i])\n        total_sum += abs(digit1 - digit2)\n\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/560", "solution": "def union_elements(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the union of elements from two given tuples and outputs them in sorted order.\n    Combines elements from both tuples, ensures uniqueness, and sorts the result.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Identify unique elements and combine into a single collection (set for uniqueness)\n    combined_elements = set(tuple1).union(set(tuple2))\n\n    # Sort the combined unique elements in ascending order\n    sorted_elements = sorted(list(combined_elements))\n\n    # Return the sorted unique elements as a tuple\n    return tuple(sorted_elements)"}
