{"task_id": "Mbpp/586", "solution": "def split_Arr(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits input_list into two parts at index n, then concatenates the second part with the first part.\n    Raises ValueError if n is out of bounds (i.e., n < 0 or n > len(input_list)).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (0 <= n <= len(input_list)):\n        raise ValueError(\"Index n is out of bounds for the given list.\")\n\n    first_part = input_list[0:n]\n    second_part = input_list[n:]\n    return second_part + first_part"}
