{"task_id": "Mbpp/619", "solution": "def move_num(input_string: str) -> str:\n    # Separates numeric characters from non-numeric characters and reorders them.\n    # All numbers are moved to the end, preserving relative order within both groups.\n    non_digits_list = []\n    digits_list = []\n\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char.isdigit():\n            digits_list.append(char)\n        else:\n            non_digits_list.append(char)\n\n    return \"\".join(non_digits_list) + \"\".join(digits_list)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list[int], list2: list[int], size: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    The function iterates through both lists to find the two middle elements of the combined sorted set.\n    \"\"\"\n    i = 0  # Pointer for list1\n    j = 0  # Pointer for list2\n    m1 = -1  # Stores the (size)-th element\n    m2 = -1  # Stores the (size+1)-th element\n\n    # Iterate up to size+1 times to find the two middle elements (at 0-indexed positions size-1 and size)\n    for count in range(size + 1):\n        # Handle cases where one list is exhausted\n        if i == size:\n            current_element = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n        elif j == size:\n            current_element = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        # Compare elements from both lists and pick the smaller one\n        elif list1[i] <= list2[j]:\n            current_element = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            current_element = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n\n        # Store the elements at the median positions\n        if count == size - 1:\n            m1 = current_element\n        if count == size:\n            m2 = current_element\n\n    return (m1 + m2) / 2.0"}
