{"task_id": "Mbpp/632", "solution": "def move_zero(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Moves all zeroes to the end of the given list while preserving the relative order of non-zero elements.\n    Returns a new list with the reordered elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    non_zero_elements = []\n    zero_count = 0\n    for element in input_list:\n        if element == 0:\n            zero_count += 1\n        else:\n            non_zero_elements.append(element)\n    return non_zero_elements + [0] * zero_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/633", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef pair_xor_Sum(numbers: List[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of bitwise XOR of all unique pairs in a given list of numbers.\n\n    Iterates through all unique pairs and accumulates their XOR sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_xor_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            total_xor_sum += (numbers[i] ^ numbers[j])\n    return total_xor_sum"}
