{"task_id": "Mbpp/724", "solution": "class PowerBaseSumCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates the logic for computing base raised to power and then summing the digits of the result.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, base: int, power: int):\n        self._base: int = base\n        self._power: int = power\n        self._power_result_str: str = \"\"\n        self._sum_of_digits: int = 0\n\n    def _calculate_power(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Computes base^power and returns its string representation.\"\"\"\n        result = self._base ** self._power\n        self._power_result_str = str(result)\n        return self._power_result_str\n\n    def _calculate_sum_of_digits(self, power_result_str: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of digits from the given string representation of the power result.\"\"\"\n        total_sum = sum(int(digit) for digit in power_result_str)\n        self._sum_of_digits = total_sum\n        return total_sum\n\n    def get_sum_of_digits(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Triggers the calculation and returns the final sum of digits.\"\"\"\n        power_str = self._calculate_power()\n        return self._calculate_sum_of_digits(power_str)\n\ndef power_base_sum(base: int, power: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all digits of the base to the specified power.\n    This function delegates the core calculation to an internal calculator class.\n    \"\"\"\n    calculator = PowerBaseSumCalculator(base, power)\n    return calculator.get_sum_of_digits()"}
