{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def sum_in_range(l, r):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    Natural numbers are considered to start from 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    if l > r:\n        return 0\n\n    # Natural numbers start from 1, so the effective lower bound is max(1, l)\n    start = max(1, l)\n\n    for num in range(start, r + 1):\n        if num % 2 != 0:  # Check if the number is odd\n            total_sum += num\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(array: list, element: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the index of the last occurrence, or -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid  # Found a potential last occurrence\n            low = mid + 1  # Search in the right half for a later occurrence\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # array[mid] > element\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result"}
