{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of the number left by d positions, assuming a 32-bit representation.\n    Bits shifted out from the left are wrapped around to the right.\n    \"\"\"\n    BITS = 32\n    # Normalize the rotation amount to be within [0, BITS-1]\n    d_normalized = d % BITS\n\n    # Perform the left shift\n    shifted_left = number << d_normalized\n\n    # Get the bits that wrapped around from the left\n    wrapped_bits = number >> (BITS - d_normalized)\n\n    # Combine the shifted bits and the wrapped-around bits\n    rotated_number = shifted_left | wrapped_bits\n\n    # Ensure the result is strictly 32-bit by masking\n    # 0xFFFFFFFF is a 32-bit mask (all ones)\n    return rotated_number & 0xFFFFFFFF"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/805", "solution": "from typing import List, Union\n\ndef max_sum_list(list_of_lists: List[List[Union[int, float]]]) -> List[Union[int, float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the sub-list within a list of lists whose elements sum to the highest value.\n    If the input list is empty, it returns an empty list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return []\n\n    max_sum = float('-inf')\n    result_list = []\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        current_sum = sum(sublist)\n        if current_sum > max_sum:\n            max_sum = current_sum\n            result_list = sublist\n\n    return result_list"}
